WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.960
- All right everybody,
we've reached the point

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.850
where I share something to bring you joy

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:05.300
from the world of social media.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.657
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:06.657 --> 00:00:07.531
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.531 --> 00:00:10.300
(audience applause)

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.700
This story starts with the Compton woman

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.730
who completely turned her life around.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:17.260
She had her first child
at 15 and another at 19,

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.320
and ended up relying on welfare,

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.990
but it wasn't the life she'd hoped for,

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:22.580
so she made some changes.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.210
Thank goodness because 30 years later,

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.930
she's a registered nurse who
served on the front lines

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.390
in the battle against COVID.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:31.180
She even went to help in
New York for a few months

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.540
and now she's back in
L.A. taking to the streets

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.670
to provide her neighbors with resources,

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.630
to not only prevent coronavirus,

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:39.910
but to live their healthiest lives.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.683
From Street Love, please
everybody welcome Shannon.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.851
(audience cheers)

00:00:46.851 --> 00:00:50.000
I love your dress or your
top, whatever that is,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.420
that's beautiful, I love your outfit.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.300
- Thank you for having me on your show.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.500
- No absolutely, we're so
happy that you're here.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.270
So Shannon, this is an
amazing turnaround story.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.390
Why did you want to be a nurse?

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:05.130
- Well it started when I had
my first son at the age of 15

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.350
and I had a mentor,

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.800
who to today we are
still very good friends.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.140
She was a registered nurse

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.180
and she taught our nursing program

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.380
that coupled with my nurturing spirit,

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:17.320
it was destined to be.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:18.153
- That's amazing.

00:01:18.153 --> 00:01:19.390
Well thank you so much, first of all,

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:21.700
for everything that you did on
the front lines for all of us

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.218
and are still doing, thank you so much.

00:01:24.218 --> 00:01:25.639
(audience applause)

00:01:25.639 --> 00:01:28.490
So tell us what Street
Love does for communities

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:29.363
in Los Angeles.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:33.200
- Well I started Street
Love after coming back

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.380
from New York working on the
front line with the COVID

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:40.180
and seeing the real
need of how the disease

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.030
impacted people that had co-morbidities

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:45.500
and it was very important
for me to give back

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.860
to the communities,

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.550
such as Compton and Watts and Carson

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:51.690
and other Los Angeles areas.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.820
And we go in and give the
health and wellness message,

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.670
as well as give health
and wellness resources,

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:00.610
such as wellness boxes,
blood pressure cuffs,

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:03.740
wellness journals, all
different types of things.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:07.830
We educated on COVID and
hand hygiene and face masks

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:11.150
and our goal is to take this
not only from city to city,

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.000
in California, but state to state.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.580
- That's amazing.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.210
Well thank you so much for
everything you're doing Shannon.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:21.503
I'm liking your post right now, all right?

00:02:21.503 --> 00:02:22.336
(audience applause)

00:02:22.336 --> 00:02:25.190
- Thank you so much for
having me, I love your show.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.170
- Oh, thank you so much,
but hey, that's not all.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:28.960
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.680
that go-to pen at "The
Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:34.200
wants to honor ultimate
overachievers, just like you ma'am.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.420
So they'll be using their G2 gel ink pen

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.100
to write you a check for
$1,000 How's that sound?

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:39.933
(audience cheers)

00:02:39.933 --> 00:02:41.016
- Oh my god.

